WEBVTT

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:32.960
See you next time.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:10.660
It's a resistance.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.870
It looks like it.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.340
Do you think it's an ally?

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.760
I don't think it's a heavy attack.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:22.450
Let's talk about it.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:24.570
It seems to have that feeling.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.490
If you fall well, you'll be saved in various ways.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:31.640
Please do the rest.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:47.550
Oh, my.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.230
This customer seems to have a habit.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:54.820
I'm not very good at this, though.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.480
Should I say thank you for your help?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.800
It's the 8th Fleet of the Earth Army, Marius Lamius.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:24.650
Didn't the 8th Fleet go extinct?

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:29.580
We're going to...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.350
My name is Ashima Saibu. I'm from the desert.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:34.730
I don't need any thanks.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:38.740
You know, right? I didn't save you guys.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.700
I didn't even shoot my enemy.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.660
You've been doing this to a tiger in the desert?

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.980
I've seen your face somewhere.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.420
Mura Fura. I don't know anyone around here.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.910
Endymion's Takata.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.220
I didn't expect to meet you in such a place.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.500
You have a lot of information, don't you?

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.250
About us, too?

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.860
Archangel, the new special officer of the old army.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.030
He was chased by the crew and fled to Earth.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.630
And that's...

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.650
X-105 Strike.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.940
It's a prototype of the Earth Army's new mobile weapon.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.360
Well, then...

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:37.780
I'm glad we both know who it is, but I'm surprised that such a disaster has come to us.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:44.800
It's an accident that I ended up here, but I'd like to ask you what you're going to do from now on.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:51.340
Can you become a shell?

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:57.900
If you're going to talk, put the gun down first.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.140
And the pilot of that one too.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:01.720
Understood.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:08.380
Major Yamada, come down here.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:28.470
Are you crazy?

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:31.840
Oh, you?

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:52.830
Why are you so...

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:05.720
You were at the morgue at that time.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:08.380
Let go of me, you idiot!

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:19.080
What's going on?

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.780
I heard that both of you entered Gibraltar safely, so I'm relieved.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.180
Thank you for your hard work in the previous battle.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:47.300
I almost died, but...

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.540
Unfortunately, we were unable to defeat Ashitsuki and Strike,

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:56.570
but it may be a good thing that you guys got off together, even though you were not willing to.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:59.980
Ashitsuki will be a part of the Earth's mid-range forces in the future.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.010
You may be our target, but for a while, stay in Gibraltar and follow them.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:11.460
If you have a chance, shoot them.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.460
So you're telling me to go back to the sky?

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:23.140
You're telling us, the middle-class army, to look for a foothold and go around the ground?

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.000
Huh?

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:29.010
Hey, you!

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:36.890
If I have a chance, I'll shoot you.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:39.150
Next time, I'll be sure to do it.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:59.050
This is a guest.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:00.610
Take good care of it.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:06.700
Roger.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.230
You live in a place like this?

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.800
This is the front line base.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.640
Everyone's house is in the city.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:41.540
It hasn't been burned yet.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:43.180
City?

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:47.180
There are people from Tashil, Muura, and Vanadia.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:51.480
We are a group of city heroes.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.410
How about coffee?

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:56.120
Thank you.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.600
Use whatever you like.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:05.110
Oh, the ship was saved, too.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:12.860
I want to hear from you, Saib.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:14.660
But it's not here.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.110
If it's them, I don't think it's a problem to put them in the camp.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.810
What about her?

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:27.640
She's the goddess of our victory.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.260
So, what's your name?

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:31.660
Huh?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.310
If you're a goddess, you should know.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:42.100
My name is Yura Kagari.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:47.240
So you guys want to go to Alaska, right?

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:55.160
Thank you for your hard work.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:56.200
Yeah.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:57.310
Yeah.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:09.270
I'm sorry about earlier. I didn't mean to hit you.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.560
Well, it's not like that.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:16.190
That's Hazumi. Forgive me.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.350
What's so funny?

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.660
Well, I mean...

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:25.300
I was worried.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:29.400
I wondered what happened to you after that.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:42.350
I'm going over there.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:43.610
It's okay.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:51.320
But I can't believe I'm going to be on something like this.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:59.690
And now I'm on Earth.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:06.260
There were a lot of things.

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:13.700
Why are you here?

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:17.160
Weren't you Obu's child?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:40.500
Well, even if it's the ZAFT's power, it's this kind of land.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:42.610
There's no way there's an army in the desert.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:48.060
But three days ago, the Victoria Space Base was dropped here.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.900
Their momentum is strong.

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:53.530
Victoria? Three days ago?

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:54.600
Oh my.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:05.170
Here, the African Union is originally from Poland.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:11.280
The South African Union of South Africa, which was doing its best, was finally abandoned by the Earth's army.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.970
The line is changing day by day.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:19.360
You guys are doing your best in that.

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:29.440
From our point of view...

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:34.080
It's the earth army. They control both and just come to take it.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:40.760
What about that ship in the atmosphere?

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.580
I can't take that altitude.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:48.400
If you can't cross the mountain range, you'll have to leave Gibraltar.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.870
With this force? Don't say nonsense.

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:59.590
I'll do my best to get out of the high seas and go from the Indian Ocean to the Pacific Ocean.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.740
It's the Pacific Ocean.

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:06.280
It's not a distance you can go at once without securing a respite route.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:11.210
The Sunbeam Alliance is completely a force of the ZAFT, right?

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:13.710
Is the Sekido Alliance still neutral?

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.070
Hey, hey, you're quick-witted.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.030
Are you already worried about that?

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:23.900
There's a Decepticon here in Panadia.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.280
Oh, do you mean to do your best and get out?

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:37.140
It's me, Takotsuta.

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:37.580
Hmm?

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.800
Excuse me.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:47.630
Captain, do you have a cold?

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.800
Did you come all the way here to tell me that?

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.880
N-No, that's not what I meant.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:56.390
I'm ready to go.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:56.960
Yes.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:02.270
I didn't want to do anything too hard, though.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.980
Well, I guess I can't help it.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:06.480
Nice.

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:15.760
This time, I added a little bit of powder, but this is good too.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:29.620
To be in the Resistance base...

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:34.030
I feel like the story is going in a strange direction more and more.

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:36.360
Oh, it's a desert.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:41.320
Oh, if it's like this, I didn't say I'd stay at that time.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:46.320
But if you were riding a shuttle there, you'd be dead by now.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:50.380
I'm sure it's going to be.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:02.310
What about you, Kira?

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:11.150
From now on, we will attack the resistance base.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.500
Last night, Oita went too far.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.800
We have to teach the bad guys a lesson.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:20.260
The target is Tassel.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.830
All units, appear!

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.400
Oh, what are you doing again?

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:50.190
I was playing around with the installation pressure at the battle last night, so I'm adjusting it.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:54.380
Oh, I see. You're a convenient pilot.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:58.800
You're kind of motivated, aren't you?

00:16:58.800 --> 00:16:59.980
Yamato Shou-

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.790
Hahahahaha

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:08.420
If we don't do it, there's nothing we can do.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:13.320
If I don't do my best and throw it hard, this ship will...

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:19.570
Kakari, what are you doing?

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:20.860
It's your turn.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:22.810
Oh, yeah.

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:27.900
Did you see the pilot of the mobile suit of the Japanese army?

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:29.420
No.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:29.840
Everyone

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:30.960
Do you need something?

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:36.040
It's not that I need it, but I forgot to ask your name again.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.680
Eh? Weren't you an acquaintance?

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:45.910
Ah, that's right. When you say acquaintance, it's an acquaintance.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:46.970
Kagari.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:53.280
Yes, Afumero.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:53.820
Ah.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.860
Please be careful. You'll get caught.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.220
I'm sorry.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:06.960
You won't be able to see what's around you.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.340
Shut up!

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:20.180
It's time for you to go to sleep.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.660
I'll have you sleep forever.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:25.590
I won't say anything.

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:27.520
I'm Keiko.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.920
We'll start the attack in 15 minutes.

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:34.750
Come on, hurry up and go.

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:52.520
Wait a minute, Frey!

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.960
I don't know about that!

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.460
Shut up!

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.580
Stop it already!

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:04.370
Hey, what are you doing?

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.910
Wait a minute.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:24.710
I'm talking to you.

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.760
It has nothing to do with Kira.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.150
It has nothing to do with me!

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:32.710
I hate you!

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:45.130
I'm tired of the battle.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.940
I can't stop.

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:57.280
I'm tired of the battle.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:08.040
If you really fight, you won't be able to win me over.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:28.310
You've been with me all this time. You've held me tight.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:34.200
No one cares what kind of feelings I've been fighting to protect me!

00:22:05.084 --> 00:22:05.744
Um...

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:31.910
Please subscribe to my channel.

00:23:22.240 --> 00:23:29.850
Archangels entered the Resistance base in search of a way to escape, but the desert tiger, Waldfeld, is blocking their way.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.940
Is the flame that burns the sky a punishment for repeated battles?

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:38.290
The mind that delusions is mercilessly fighting the enemy.

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:40.240
The effect is a new spark.

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:43.580
Next time on Mobile Suit Gundam SEED.

00:23:43.580 --> 00:23:44.690
Payback!

00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:48.310
With a critical blow, cut off the Gundam!
